# =============================================================================
# ALERT -> LIBRARY RISK  **DIRECT** LINKAGE   (no RSM / RGL route)
#
# THE STORY THIS PIPELINE TELLS:
#   The RSM lane asks: "of the risks sitting under the summaries this alert was
#   linked to, which ones does the alert bear on?" That route caps recall at
#   upstream RSM recall (89.1%) and never shows the model 131 golden links.
#   Here we delete the route. Every alert is judged against EVERY published
#   library risk in Helios. NOT_JUDGED should therefore be 0, the denominator
#   becomes the FULL addressable golden, and the two lanes become comparable on
#   the same base.
#
# WHAT IS DELIBERATELY UNCHANGED FROM `lr_linkage_full.py` (so the head-to-head
# in [F0] is a clean single-variable experiment):
#   [A] data load, risk_text, load_alerts     - verbatim
#   [B1] LANE, RISK_SCHEMA, prompt file       - verbatim
#   judge machinery (chunk / semaphore / 401) - verbatim
#   [D] risk_scorecard                        - verbatim
#   [F] [F1] [F2]                             - reuse from lr_linkage_full.py
#   ONLY the candidate source changes. That is the whole experiment.
#
# CRASH SAFETY (VDI disconnects):
#   Work unit = (RECORD_ID, chunk_index). The unit plan is written to disk
#   BEFORE any model call and never rebuilt on resume, so a re-embed or a new
#   Helios row cannot shift chunk boundaries and orphan completed work. Every
#   finished unit is appended to a fsync'd JSONL; a parquet snapshot lands every
#   SNAPSHOT_EVERY units. After a disconnect: re-run cells [0] -> [C] and it
#   picks up exactly where it stopped.
#
# SECTIONS
#   0.   Imports + paths
#   A.   Data load                        (verbatim from the RSM lane)
#   A1.  SCOPE RECOVERY                   <- pins the SAME 160 records
#   A2.  Validation probe
#   B1.  Config + model params + checkpoint config
#   B2.  Reachability (direct)
#   C.   Work plan + checkpointed model execution
#   D.   Performance scorecard            (verbatim from the RSM lane)
#   E.   Diagnostic (direct)
#   F0.  Head-to-head vs the RSM route
#   F/F1/F2 -> reuse lr_linkage_full.py unchanged
# =============================================================================


